      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-48936",
      ":question/problem": "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = t^{2} - t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $2$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
